\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces This scatter plot illustrates the relationship between parallax and distance for NGC 6383. The distribution of parallax values is presented as a histogram (orange) and a kernel density estimate (violet), highlighting the underlying density of measurements. Similarly, the distribution of distance estimates is shown as a histogram (orange) and a kernel density estimate (violet). The mean parallax ($\mu _\varpi $) is represented by the dashed blue line, along with its uncertainty. The mean distance ($d$) is depicted by the dashed blue line, also with its associated uncertainty. The data points of NGC 6383 sources are displayed as scattered points, where their parallax is plotted against their $G_{\textrm  {mag}}$ magnitude. The color of each point indicates the probability assigned to the source. The green star marker and error bar represent the parallax and $G_{\textrm  {mag}}$ magnitude of HD 159176.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:parallax}{{2}{4}{This scatter plot illustrates the relationship between parallax and distance for NGC 6383. The distribution of parallax values is presented as a histogram (orange) and a kernel density estimate (violet), highlighting the underlying density of measurements. Similarly, the distribution of distance estimates is shown as a histogram (orange) and a kernel density estimate (violet). The mean parallax ($\mu _\varpi $) is represented by the dashed blue line, along with its uncertainty. The mean distance ($d$) is depicted by the dashed blue line, also with its associated uncertainty. The data points of NGC 6383 sources are displayed as scattered points, where their parallax is plotted against their $G_{\textrm {mag}}$ magnitude. The color of each point indicates the probability assigned to the source. The green star marker and error bar represent the parallax and $G_{\textrm {mag}}$ magnitude of HD 159176}{figure.2}{}}
