\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces This figure illustrates the density profiles of the cluster based on the 2-parameter and 3-parameter King models, utilizing the obtained parameters. The black points represent the observed density profile (RDP), with error bars denoting the associated uncertainties. The fuchsia curve represents the 3-parameter King model, while the blue curve represents the 2-parameter King model. The $x$-axis represents the radial distance ($r$) in arcminutes, and the $y$-axis represents the stellar density ($\rho $) in units of stars per square arcminute. The shaded region around the 3-parameter King model curve indicates the uncertainty range. Red dashed lines indicate the estimated core radius ($R_c$), tidal radius ($R_t$), and cluster radius ($R_{cl}$). The green dashed line represents the mean background density ($b$).}}{6}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:king}{{5}{6}{This figure illustrates the density profiles of the cluster based on the 2-parameter and 3-parameter King models, utilizing the obtained parameters. The black points represent the observed density profile (RDP), with error bars denoting the associated uncertainties. The fuchsia curve represents the 3-parameter King model, while the blue curve represents the 2-parameter King model. The $x$-axis represents the radial distance ($r$) in arcminutes, and the $y$-axis represents the stellar density ($\rho $) in units of stars per square arcminute. The shaded region around the 3-parameter King model curve indicates the uncertainty range. Red dashed lines indicate the estimated core radius ($R_c$), tidal radius ($R_t$), and cluster radius ($R_{cl}$). The green dashed line represents the mean background density ($b$)}{figure.5}{}}
