\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A1}{\ignorespaces This figure displays the trace plot of the proper motion parameter $\mu $ for the Bayesian analysis. It provides insights into the posterior distribution of the proper motion parameter and allows for the assessment of convergence and uncertainty.}}{10}{figure.A1.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A2}{\ignorespaces This figure presents the trace plot and summary statistics for the two-parameter King profile obtained from the Bayesian analysis. It offers a visual representation of the posterior distribution of the parameters, along with important statistical summaries.}}{10}{figure.A1.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A3}{\ignorespaces This figure showcases the trace plot and summary statistics of the King profile parameters obtained from the Bayesian analysis. The trace plot illustrates the posterior distribution of the parameters, while the summary statistics provide key information such as mean, standard deviation, and credible intervals.}}{10}{figure.A1.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A4}{\ignorespaces This figure depicts the equatorial coordinates and proper motions of the members of the NGC 6383 open cluster. The left panel shows the scatter plot of member positions in equatorial coordinates (right ascension, $\alpha $, and declination, $\delta $). The color-coded points represent the probability of cluster membership. Error bars indicate the uncertainties in the coordinates. The right panel displays the scatter plot of proper motions ($\mu _alpha*)$ and $\mu _\delta )$ for the cluster members. Again, the color of the points corresponds to the probability of membership, and error bars represent the uncertainties in the proper motions. The colorbar on the right indicates the probability values.}}{10}{figure.A1.4}\protected@file@percent }
